              Restaurants, coffee, bars, shops, events, and one of the best areas to
              get a feel for Redmond’s growth.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="card">
            <h3>Dry Canyon Area</h3>
            <p>
              Popular for walking, biking, parks, sports fields, and easy outdoor time
              close to town.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="card">
            <h3>South Redmond</h3>
            <p>
              Convenient for commuting toward Bend and accessing shopping, services,
              and newer neighborhoods.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="card">
            <h3>North Redmond</h3>
            <p>
              Practical access toward Terrebonne, Smith Rock, Madras, and the airport.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="card">
            <h3>Airport Area</h3>
            <p>
              Useful for travelers, airport workers, rental cars, hotels, and quick
              regional access.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="card">
            <h3>Terrebonne Nearby</h3>
            <p>
              Not Redmond itself, but closely connected because of Smith Rock and the
              short drive north.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
