      <section class="section">
        <h2>Living in Redmond</h2>
        <p>
          Redmond has become a serious option for people who want Central Oregon access
          without being directly in Bend. It is still growing quickly, but it often feels
          more practical, more affordable, and easier to navigate.
        </p>

        <p>
          The tradeoff is that some people still drive to Bend for certain restaurants,
          jobs, events, or activities. But Redmond has its own momentum, and it continues
          becoming a stronger city on its own.
        </p>
